  "notes": "The Offshore Code Comparison, Collaboration, Continued, with Correlation (OC5) is an international research project run under the International Energy Agency (IEA) Wind Task 30. The project is focused on validating the tools used design offshore wind systems. OC5 consists of four phases.\n\n•\tPhase 2: Analysis of a scaled wind turbine on a floating semisubmersible in an ocean basin\n\nThis website provides the data used for validation in these four phases, as well as simulation results from multiple participants.",
